WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:08.000
Giants. Robots. Dragons. Gods….Clowns…&nbsp;
literally no one is safe from being taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.040
down by Monkey D. Luffy. The hero of&nbsp;
One Piece has spent decades punching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.760
some of the most punchable faces ever to&nbsp;
appear in manga and anime and today we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.360
talking about every single character that&nbsp;
Luffy has defeated throughout the story.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:29.680
And the very first thing Luffy did when he&nbsp;
set sail as a pirate was punch the lights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.480
out of the Lord of the Coast. He finally&nbsp;
got his revenge on the Sea King that took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.440
Shanks’ arm in the form of a knuckle&nbsp;
sandwich - and in doing so he finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:46.440
proved he wasn’t the same kid he used to&nbsp;
be. Luffy was ready to be a real pirate.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.160
After a poorly timed whirlpool, Luffy&nbsp;
found himself barreling toward the Alvida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.080
Pirates…literally. After meeting his most&nbsp;
pink friend and future Hero of the Marines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.680
Koby, Luffy set the unwilling cabin&nbsp;
boy free by punching his boss - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.760
most beautiful pirate on the seas other&nbsp;
than Boa Hancock - right into the sea.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.600
After that, Luffy ran into some opposition while&nbsp;
trying to recruit his first crewmate. ****A lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.320
fans remember Luffy fighting Axe-Hand Morgan&nbsp;
after freeing Zoro on Shells Town. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:24.200
Zoro was actually the one to finish the corrupt&nbsp;
captain off. In one of the biggest low diff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:31.240
matchups of all time, Luffy actually defeats&nbsp;
Helmeppo, who was threatening Koby with a pistol.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.880
And then immediately after that battle,&nbsp;
Luffy beat up Koby, in order to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.680
the marines of Shells Town the impression&nbsp;
that they aren’t actual allies. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.680
what kind of ally would beat the snot out of one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.800
of his best friends? [whispered] (It’s the&nbsp;
kind who wants you to live out your dreams)

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:54.440
Moving over to Orange Town, Luffy came face&nbsp;
to face with the Lion Tamer Mohji and Richie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:59.840
the Lion. And while Richie probably should&nbsp;
have been caged, it was actually Luffy who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:08.800
found himself locked in a cage on this particular&nbsp;
occasion.However, nobody can keep Luffy locked up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:15.280
especially when he needs to fight on behalf&nbsp;
of Chou Chou, one of anime’s best dogs.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:22.400
Luffy couldn’t settle for simply beating&nbsp;
up Mohji. He needed to fight his boss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.280
This was Luffy’s first fight against a fellow&nbsp;
devil fruit user, making it a real challenge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.360
but once Luffy and Nami managed to&nbsp;
tie up all of Buggy’s body parts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.240
Baby Buggy didn’t stand a chance and he got&nbsp;
Gum-Gum Bazooka’d into the stratosphere.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.160
By the time the crew arrived in Syrup&nbsp;
village, Luffy had already taken out a lion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:49.960
so Certified Cat Boy Captain Kuro didn’t&nbsp;
stand a chance. Kuro’s claws were sharp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:55.920
but Luffy’s wits were sharper…Okay, that’s&nbsp;
not accurate - Luffy doesn’t have any wits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.760
His strategy was actually just so dumb it&nbsp;
actually worked. He wrapped his rubbery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.560
limbs all around Kuro so he couldn’t use&nbsp;
his speed to his advantage and then gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:13.160
him the headbutt to end all headbutts&nbsp;
in the form of a Gomu Gomu no Bell.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.520
All that Syrup Village business really worked&nbsp;
up an appetite, so Luffy and the gang’s next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.600
stop was the floating restaurant, Baratie.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, they weren’t the only ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.840
who showed up without a reservation. Along&nbsp;
came Don Krieg, who led the largest fleet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.120
in all of the East Blue. After Dracule Mihawk&nbsp;
sliced up his fleet and ships in the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:39.560
he tried to take the Baratie for himself. However,&nbsp;
despite his underhanded tactics of using poison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:46.960
spikes, cannons, and more - he couldn’t compare&nbsp;
with Luffy’s brute strength and was wiped out.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:53.960
With Don Krieg defeated, there was only one pirate&nbsp;
left in the East Blue who was more powerful and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.960 --> 00:04:01.160
infamous: Arlong. This sawshark fishman gave&nbsp;
Luffy his most difficult fight yet, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:09.120
stakes were personal. The fight ended in the map&nbsp;
room where Arlong had tortured Nami, forcing her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:17.520
to draw maps since her childhood. He brought down&nbsp;
Arlong and his entire park with a Gum Gum Axe.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:25.640
Entering the Grand Line, Luffy wouldn’t take&nbsp;
another W until Little Garden where he went up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:32.360
against the Candle Man Mr. 3 - whose real name&nbsp;
is Galdino, it turns out. Most of the crew was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:41.600
nearly turned into a Wax Museum, but Luffy Waxed&nbsp;
On and Waxed Off until Galdino was Gal-decimated.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.640
On Drum Island, Luffy dethroned&nbsp;
Wapol, a cruel king with a bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:53.440
case of the munch-munchies. This was&nbsp;
the first monarch Luffy would punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:59.600
but it certainly wouldn’t be the last and&nbsp;
in doing so he turned the Drum Kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:05.200
into a democracy when Dalton was elected the&nbsp;
leader of the newly dubbed Sakura Kingdom.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:15.840
And Luffy went from beating his first king to his&nbsp;
first Warlord, when Luffy defeated Crocodile in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:21.320
round 3 of their fight. After being knocked&nbsp;
down twice by the sand user, Luffy beat him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:27.840
up using nothing but his own blood, sweat, and&nbsp;
tears…but mostly his blood, which hardened the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:33.400
logia user’s sand and allowed him to be battered&nbsp;
right through the ceiling of the Tomb of the King.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:41.320
The crew’s next destination was Jaya, where Luffy&nbsp;
was able to demonstrate how much he’d grown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:49.440
resemble his mentor, Shanks. When Bellamy picked a&nbsp;
fight and made fun of Luffy’s dreams, he sat there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:58.000
and took it because he wasn’t worth the trouble.&nbsp;
But when Bellamy hurt one of Luffy’s friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:05.320
then Luffy got serious. The spring-spring man&nbsp;
bounced all around Jaya, but Luffy didn’t need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:12.320
to use his devil fruit at all. All it took was a&nbsp;
single punch to break Bellamy the Hyena’s spirit.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:20.840
Once Luffy and co found themselves on Skypiea,&nbsp;
they went up against Enel’s Priests. Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:28.720
helped Sanji out against Satori, but Sanji made&nbsp;
the finishing blow. Luffy’s real battle on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:36.800
island was against God. Or at least, somebody&nbsp;
who considered himself a God. Enel had never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:43.920
met an opponent who wasn’t instantly incinerated&nbsp;
by his lightning strikes, but was in for a huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:52.360
surprise when Luffy’s rubber body was completely&nbsp;
immune to his attacks. Even without his lightning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:58.480
Enel still put up quite a fight using his&nbsp;
observation haki, which he called “Mantra.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.400
However, in the end Luffy defeated him&nbsp;
and rang the bell in the City of Gold.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:10.560
The next opponent was back on the Blue Sea on&nbsp;
Long Ring Long Land, when Foxy the Silver Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.880
challenged the Straw Hats to a Davy Back&nbsp;
Fight. In the final round of the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:21.320
the two captains had a one v one match up.&nbsp;
However, Foxy’s Slow-Slow beam was so hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:28.800
to deal with that it took Luffy’s ultimate form&nbsp;
to defeat him: Afro Luffy. Despite Foxy’s tricks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:38.120
and traps, nothing could defeat the boxing&nbsp;
prowess of Afro Luffy, and he won the round.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:46.440
The next opponent was even more difficult for&nbsp;
Luffy to fight than the near- invincible Foxy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:54.000
However, this one wasn’t physically difficult,&nbsp;
it was emotionally difficult. On Water 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.760
Usopp challenged Luffy for the ownership&nbsp;
of the Going Merry, the crew’s ship that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:04.520
needed to be replaced and suffering extreme&nbsp;
damage on their adventures. Usopp used all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:10.040
of the resources and knowledge he’d gained about&nbsp;
Luffy’s weaknesses throughout their adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:15.880
but ultimately was completely&nbsp;
outclassed by his captain’s strength.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:23.480
When the crew stormed Enies Lobby, Luffy’s&nbsp;
first victim was the CP9 agent Blueno,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:28.640
who ate the Door-Door fruit. However, even for&nbsp;
someone who can make doors anywhere, there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:35.440
no escape from the insane speed of Luffy’s Gear 2.&nbsp;
The fight against Blueno was Oda’s way of showing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:42.320
off the strength of Luffy’s new Gear techniques&nbsp;
before Luffy fought his real opponent of the arc:

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:52.640
Rob Lucci. This leopard zoan fruit user&nbsp;
gave Luffy his toughest fight yet. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.880
CP9 Power House was willing to carry out&nbsp;
any order on behalf of the government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:04.720
all to satisfy his immense bloodlust.&nbsp;
Lucci devastated Luffy with the secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:11.280
techniques called the Six Powers,&nbsp;
particularly his strongest attack:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:17.840
The Rokuogan. However, Lucci finally met defeat&nbsp;
on the receiving end of Luffy’s Jet Gatling Gun.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.840
Before leaving ****Water 7, Luffy’s&nbsp;
grandpa showed up to crash the party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:26.560
leading to a quick rematch with&nbsp;
Koby. As everyone would predict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.800
Koby didn’t stand a chance - but he&nbsp;
sure is getting stronger, though!

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:36.720
Luffy’s next terrifying opponent&nbsp;
was on the horror-themed island of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.840
Thriller Bark. The Warlord Gecko Moria&nbsp;
resurrected his ultimate zombie, Oars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:47.920
from the body of a fearsome Ancient Giant. Things&nbsp;
looked bleak for the Straw Hats, but Luffy took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:55.080
a ton of shadows into his own body in order to&nbsp;
transform into Nightmare Luffy and crushed Oars.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:10:04.480
Up next was Moria himself, the next Warlord to&nbsp;
fall to Straw Hat Luffy. Even when Moria used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:10.320
Shadow’s Asgard to suck 1,000 shadows&nbsp;
into himself and boost his strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:17.920
he wasn’t able to beat Luffy. With every punch,&nbsp;
Moria spit up shadows, unable to control the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:23.480
power of so many at once. After that fight,&nbsp;
though, nothing happened on Thriller Bark.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:32.320
When the crew arrived at Sabaody Archipelago, they&nbsp;
were ready to tackle the New World. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:39.360
those plans went sideways when they went to rescue&nbsp;
their mermaid friend Camie from a slave auction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:44.840
****When the Celestial Dragon St. Charlos shoots&nbsp;
Hatchan, Luffy does the morally correct thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:49.920
that anyone should do when encountering a&nbsp;
slave owner and punches him into oblivion.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.480
After Kuma gives Luffy an all-expenses&nbsp;
paid trip to Amazon Lily, he finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.480 --> 00:11:01.120
himself in Trial by Combat against a black&nbsp;
panther. But as the real King of the Jungle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.160
Luffy showed Bacura the panther who’s boss.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:11.480
After that, Boa Hancock’s sisters Marigold&nbsp;
and Sandersonia went up against Luffy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:16.720
Luffy probably would have taken a definitive&nbsp;
victory, but the match was called off when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:21.200
Luffy went out of his way to hide the Mark of&nbsp;
the Celestial Dragons on the Gorgon Sisters’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:27.280
backs from the women of Amazon Lily,&nbsp;
thus stealing Boa’s heart for life.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:33.400
For the whole Marineford Saga, Luffy was&nbsp;
way out of his element. He took out a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:41.800
fodder in Impel Down, but he failed to take out&nbsp;
any big opponents.Luffy was truly in his L era&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:47.720
here. However, the ever-dependable Koby was there&nbsp;
as always to be taken down by Luffy in one hit.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:55.480
And technically, Luffy did&nbsp;
also knock out his own grandpa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.480 --> 00:12:01.320
Garp the Hero of the Marines. I mean, Garp&nbsp;
didn’t fight back whatsoever…but still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:07.120
he did knock him down on the&nbsp;
way to the executioner’s stand.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.560
After taking a couple years off to power up, Luffy&nbsp;
was back in business when he returned to Sabaody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:18.320
Archipelago and took out the Pacifistas that&nbsp;
used to give him trouble like they were nothing.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.200
While descending to Fishman Island,&nbsp;
Luffy made friends with a giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:26.960
kraken the only way he knows how…by&nbsp;
punching it as hard as he could.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:32.040
However, he wasn’t trying to make&nbsp;
friends when he punched Hody Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:41.560
the leader of the New Fishman Pirates as hard as&nbsp;
he could. The battle against Hody Jones proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:49.800
just how much stronger Luffy had become&nbsp;
over the timeskip. Hody Jones was powered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.360
up by an insane amount of Energy Steroids,&nbsp;
and was fighting against a fishman while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.360 --> 00:13:02.080
underwater…even though he was a devil fruit user.&nbsp;
And even with that massive handicap, Luffy took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:08.920
him out and destroyed the giant ark, the Noah,&nbsp;
with his Red Hawk and Elephant Gun techniques.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:18.720
The Straw Hats’ next destination was Punk Hazard,&nbsp;
where Luffy lost the first round to Caesar Clown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:24.600
who deprived him of oxygen using his devil fruit&nbsp;
powers. However, in round two of the fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:29.960
Luffy figures out Caesar’s trick and learns&nbsp;
the distance he has to stay away in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:37.400
keep breathing. Luffy clowns on this Clown&nbsp;
with his awesome Grizzly Magnum technique.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:44.600
After Punk Hazard, Luffy partnered up with&nbsp;
Trafalgar Law and the allies went to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:52.040
down Doflamingo. Well, actually they went to&nbsp;
destroy the Smile factory so that Kaidou would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:57.880
take down Doflamingo, but we all know how&nbsp;
well Luffy can follow a plan. So instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:03.080
Oda brought us to a gladiator match where&nbsp;
a suspiciously familiar contestant named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:08.320
Lucy fought to try to get the Mera&nbsp;
Mera no Mi that once belonged to Ace.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:14.920
At the coliseum, Lucy, who was shockingly&nbsp;
revealed to be Luffy in disguise easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:19.520
brought down the giant Hajrudin, who&nbsp;
would go on to join his Grand Fleet.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:25.080
He also fought an old pirate named Don Chinjao&nbsp;
who was once a rival of Luffy’s grandpa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:30.480
Garp. Despite Luffy having nothing to do with&nbsp;
that old conflict, Chinjao held a grudge and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:36.080
wanted to take it out on Luffy. This gave&nbsp;
Luffy a chance to practice his conqueror’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:43.000
haki and with a powerful punch, he gave Don&nbsp;
Chinjao the pointy head he missed so much back.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:49.440
After Chinjao, though, came the first&nbsp;
real test of Luffy’s strength since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:55.160
timeskip. Everyone Luffy fought to this&nbsp;
point, he hadn’t had to give his all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.160 --> 00:15:01.640
but Doflamingo pushed him to the limit, forcing&nbsp;
him to reveal his new ultimate technique:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:08.000
Gear 4. Base Luffy couldn’t keep up with&nbsp;
Doflamingo’s crazy strength and speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:13.800
but once he transformed into Gear 4, Bounce&nbsp;
Man wiped the smile off of Doflamingo’s face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:18.440
and he defeated the Celestial Dragon and&nbsp;
ended his terrible reign over Dressrosa.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:19.040
Cracker

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:24.600
After Dressrosa, the crew set their eyes on&nbsp;
the Four Emperors. In order to save Sanji,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.320
Luffy invaded Big Mom’s territory of Whole&nbsp;
Cake Island. In order to get him back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:34.760
Luffy had to take down two of her&nbsp;
Sweet Commanders. First was Cracker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:38.280
the warrior who fought with hardened&nbsp;
biscuit soldiers. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:43.880
Cracker couldn’t make enough biscuits to deal&nbsp;
with Luffy’s appetite. After eating his fill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:49.400
Luffy used those extra calories to turn&nbsp;
into Tank Man, and Cracker got cooked.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.080
Katakuri

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.720
Luffy’s hardest fight yet, though, came in the&nbsp;
form of Katakuri - the future sight master who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.720 --> 00:16:03.880
could predict his every move. Katakuri’s stretchy&nbsp;
mochi fruit gave him the mirror image of Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:10.080
own powers, which was fitting since their&nbsp;
fight took place in the mirror world. Over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:15.360
the course of their long battle, Luffy developed&nbsp;
his observation haki, allowing him to see briefly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:20.520
into the future. The battle almost ended in a&nbsp;
draw, with both fighters seemingly down for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:24.760
count, but Luffy was able to get back up and&nbsp;
escape Whole Cake Island with his crewmates.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:35.320
In act I of Wano, Luffy’s first&nbsp;
opponent was the Sumo champion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:41.360
Urashima. Despite Urashima’s superior&nbsp;
weight class, he was no match for Luffy.

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:46.920
This lion-bellied Gifter on Kaidou’s crew was&nbsp;
also outclassed by Luffy, who defeated him with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:52.920
a Red Hawk attack, reminding O’Tama of Luffy’s&nbsp;
brother Ace. Of course, none of these battles on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.920 --> 00:17:00.240
Wano really required Luffy to go all out. None&nbsp;
except the person you’ve all been waiting for:

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:07.640
Kaidou: The World’s Strongest Creature&nbsp;
gave Luffy the fight of his life. Kaidou’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:14.480
draconic transformation and command of advanced&nbsp;
conqueror’s haki made this emperor more powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:21.840
than any foe Luffy had fought before. In fact,&nbsp;
Kaidou was so strong that he defeated him twice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:29.640
and then seemingly literally killed him after&nbsp;
that. Unfortunately for Kaidou, that led to Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:37.680
awakening his devil fruit. After that Gear 5 Luffy&nbsp;
went Looney Tunes, using dragon form Kaidou as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:43.920
jump rope and sending the King of Beasts to the&nbsp;
magma beneath Wano’s Mt. Fuji. With this battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:51.440
Luffy truly became Joyboy’s successor and earned&nbsp;
his title as one of the Four Emperors of the Sea.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:59.160
After the Land of Wano, the crew headed to Egghead&nbsp;
Island where they reunited with some old rivals:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:05.920
Rob Lucci and Kaku, who had been promoted&nbsp;
to CP0. These guys seem to fail upward just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:11.640
as much as Buggy. Even though Rob Lucci had&nbsp;
also awakened his zoan fruit just like Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:16.960
he just couldn’t keep up with the&nbsp;
wild abilities of Gear 5 and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:21.160
at a disadvantage when Stussy ended&nbsp;
the fight by putting Lucci to sleep.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:30.440
A much more suitable opponent for Gear 5 Luffy&nbsp;
is the admiral who showed up after CP0: Kizaru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:35.680
who demolished the crew alongside Kuma two&nbsp;
years prior at Sabaody Archipelago. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:40.800
now Gear 5 Luffy can fight the Light&nbsp;
Fruit user on roughly equal footing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:45.960
the match ending essentially in a&nbsp;
draw with both fighters immobilized.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:54.800
But if this match was a tie, what about the&nbsp;
matches that Luffy outright lost? Most of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:59.080
time through sheer willpower, Luffy is&nbsp;
able to pull ahead and beat characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:03.440
many times stronger than himself. However,&nbsp;
on surprisingly numerous occasions on One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:09.920
Piece he’s been fully and utterly defeated.&nbsp;
How many times? And by who? Well, you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:17.040
find out exactly when and how Luffy has lost&nbsp;
throughout the series in this video right here.

